  HAZARD [Caution] (L0): strong acid dissolves this metal, releasing hydrogen gas which is flammable; Any metal above hydrogen in the activity series gives off hydrogen gas in acid; magnesium ribbon in hydrochloric acid is the school version, where the gas pops with a lit splint. The gas is genuinely flammable whichever metal and acid made it.
